# For LOCAL dev only. The deployed boxes get NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE and the Ello
# vars below from GitHub Actions repo Variables/Secrets (Settings > Secrets and
# variables > Actions, prefixed WEBSITE_*), passed as --build-arg in
# .github/workflows/deploy*.yml — update values there, not by editing a
# .env.local file on a box. (The Upshot IDs have built-in defaults, so CI needs no values for them.)

# ── Ello voice-navigation widget ──
# Copy to .env.local and restart the dev server. Without these the widget
# disables itself (a dev-only notice appears bottom-right saying so).
#
# These are the Ello DEV values, verified working 2026-07-31: publish returns
# 200, the socket opens, client-tools-ack is received and the agent speaks.
#
# The *-stage hosts previously listed here do NOT work —
# connect-in.getello.ai does not resolve, so the socket dies with code 1006
# while the HTTPS publish call still succeeds. That combination looks like a
# client bug and is easy to lose hours to. Use dev unless someone confirms a
# working stage host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELLO_API_KEY=ak_REPLACE_ME.setViaEnvOrDashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELLO_ASSISTANT_ID=6a64d273a4fc43f6203cd3cc
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELLO_API_BASE=https://api-in.getello.ai
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELLO_WS_URL=wss://connect-in.getello.ai/ws-ello

# ── Upshot Web SDK (in-app messages, surveys, activities, mini-games) ──
# The website is its own Upshot app. Its App SDK ID + Account ID are the built-in
# defaults in src/config/upshot.ts, so NOTHING needs setting for it to work.
# Set these only to point a build at a different Upshot app (e.g. staging):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UPSHOT_APP_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UPSHOT_OWNER_ID=
# Set to "true" to stop the SDK loading at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UPSHOT_DISABLED=true
# Leave empty. v1.4 only accepts "usa"; the region the data goes to comes back
# from Upshot's own init response (verified: an India account is routed to api.in.goupshot.com).
NEXT_PUBLIC_UPSHOT_DATA_REGION=
# Override only if Upshot give you a different CDN build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UPSHOT_SDK_URL=https://cdn.goupshot.com/UpshotWebSDK/v1.4/upshot.min.js
